  "prompts": [
    "Bound the backlog of an in-process worker queue so producers wait when it fills.",
    "Close the queue, wake blocked producers and consumers, and finish work already accepted."
  ],
  "invariant": "The same condition lock protects capacity and closure. Close rejects future puts and permits gets until the queue is empty.",
  "mantra": "Wait on state; close wakes everyone; drain before exit.",
  "pitfalls": [
    "A notification is a reason to recheck the predicate, not proof that it is still true.",
    "On a shared condition, notify() could wake the wrong kind of waiter. Separate conditions can reduce unnecessary wakeups.",
    "Checking closed before checking for queued items would discard accepted work."
  ],
